    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39863" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quā^drĭēris</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quā^t-</span></b> ),
			is, f.
		vox hibr. from quattuor and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρω,</span>
			analog. to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριήρης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a vessel having four
				banks of oars</i>, <i>a quadrireme</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">EX CLASS. PR. MIS. QVADRIERE FIDE,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Murat. 876, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quatrieris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Not. Tir. p. 177</span></i>
			.</div>
